/godot/pull/120865#issuecomment-4928333089","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120865","id":4928333089,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJcBlIQ","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-09T18:32:22Z","updated_at":"2026-07-09T18:32:22Z","body":"> The vertical scroll is overlapping while in other docks such as the file system is not.\r\n\r\nOh, you mean this?\r\n<img width=\"257\" height=\"46\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f54d4523-0c3c-4cf5-bf18-03cc6df2e302\" />\r\n\r\nThis seems like a quirk that needs to be handled in the `Tree` node itself, unrelated to this PR.\r\n\r\n> The horizontal scroll stays inside the margin and doesn't overlap with low spacings, but as spacing increases it progressively overlaps the Nodes.\r\n\r\nAgain, `Tree` stuff.\r\n\r\nAnd about the extra borders stuff, it's because since there no spacing, the borders and elements collide by a pixel. I personally see this as a non-issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/